<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73833" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμό-σπορος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sown together :</i> hence,
				<i>sprung from the same parents</i> or <i>ancestors, kindred,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				85
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				5.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				932
			</span></i>(lyr.), etc.: as Subst., <i>brother,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				611
			</span></i> ; <i>sister,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				242
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				212
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				695
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. γυνή</span> a wife <i>common to
			two</i> (Laïus and Oedipus), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				260
			</span></i> ; also of Oedipus, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ πατρὸς
				ὁμόσπορος</span>
			<i>having the same wife with</i> his father, ib.<i><span class="en">
				460
			</span></i>.</div>
